{"id":"rdd56","designation":"RDD 56","title":"Track File for JPEG 2000 Codestreams with Time-Synchronous Metadata","state":"active","suite":null,"official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/rdd56/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/rdd56/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"JPEG 2000 is a picture-by-picture compression coding defined by ISO/IEC 15444-1 and used for both individual pictures and picture sequences. Extensible Markup Language (XML) is a structured encoding for text with markup. This document specifies the mapping of JPEG 2000 codestreams and time-synchronous XML metadata into a single File Package, compatible with the MXF generic container, in a frame-wrapped configuration. Clip wrapping is not supported. This document defines the data structure at the signal interfaces of networks or storage media. This document does not define internal storage formats for MXF compliant devices.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Overview (Informative)","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 Terms and Definitions","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 PHDR Track File","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 constrained XML document","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 static XML document","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"6 PHDR Track File","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 Overall","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 General Constraints","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 Wrapping","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.4 Essence Sub Descriptors","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.5 Essence Coding","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.6 Static XML Document Instances","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.7 Indexing","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"7 PHDRMetadataTrackSubDescriptor","page":6}],"definitions":[{"term":"PHDR Track File","definition":"a Track File that interleaves JPEG 2000 codestreams with time-synchronous metadata as an extension of"}],"keywords":[{"ter